{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788462127,"nonce":"vt+q81R2HIdB2lqhhqwmAtys2MA=","title":"No verb for ideology roles or rituals — costs ~9 mood per colonist with no lever","message":"`rwa verbs` returns nothing matching ideo, role or ritual. The observation surface has no `pawn {sections:['ideo']}` either (git-bug for that is already noted in the run contract's known-gaps list), so precepts driving mood are invisible AND unfixable.\n\nMEASURED COST, colony Andbourne, Winter 14, save winter-d11-sinn-accepted:\n`pawn {id:18294, sections:['mood']}` on John returns, among ten thoughts:\n\n  No Cleric                -5\n  Missing Nocic Symbol     -4\n  Conversion resentment    -4\n\nThat is -13 on one pawn, and the same ideology thoughts sit on the rest of the roster. John was at mood 29 against a minor-break threshold of 35 and a major of 20. Two of the three are things the PLAYER fixes in one click and the agent cannot touch at all:\n\n- **Roles.** The game raised 'Councillor role activated' (3 Realitists reached) and its own letter says how: 'use the person's Social tab, or select a ritual spot or altar and press Begin role change'. Both are UI routes. `Alert_RolesEmpty` had been muted at 3 colonists with a release condition of 'roster reaches 5+'; the roster is now 6, the condition fired, and releasing the alert changed nothing because there is no verb behind it.\n- **Ideology buildings.** `Alert_IdeoBuildingMissing` names 'Nocic Symbol desired'. Without an ideo section there is no way to learn the required def from the protocol, so even `build` cannot be aimed at it.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS BEYOND MOOD: a run graded on colony outcomes has a standing, compounding, colony-wide penalty that the agent can observe the SYMPTOM of (a thought row) but cannot diagnose (no precept list) or act on (no verb). It reads as the agent mismanaging mood.\n\nACCEPTANCE:\n- `pawn {sections:['ideo']}` publishes the pawn's ideo, its role (or null), and the precepts currently generating thoughts, with each precept's mood offset.\n- A verb assigns an ideology role to a pawn, reproducing the Social tab's own gate (Ideo.RolesListForReading / Precept_Role.RequirementsMet) and REFUSING with the named unmet requirement rather than silently failing — same standard as `build`'s `selectable`.\n- The ideology-building requirement is discoverable: either an `ideo` section field naming the wanted ThingDef, or `Alert_IdeoBuildingMissing` resolved to a def that `build` accepts.\n- On this save, filling the Cleric/Councillor role removes the 'No Cleric' thought from every colonist, verified by re-reading `pawn {sections:['mood']}`.","files":null}]}